    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-8 italic">Effective Date: <time datetime="2026-10-23">October 23, 2026</time></p>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert prose-indigo max-w-none space-y-8">

      <div class="bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/20 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-6 rounded-r-xl mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-400 text-lg font-bold mt-0 flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg class="size-5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400" width="20" height="20" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.9998 9.00006V12.7501M2.69653 16.1257C1.83114 17.6257 2.91371 19.5001 4.64544 19.5001H19.3541C21.0858 19.5001 22.1684 17.6257 21.303 16.1257L13.9487 3.37819C13.0828 1.87736 10.9167 1.87736 10.0509 3.37819L2.69653 16.1257ZM11.9998 15.7501H12.0073V15.7576H11.9998V15.7501Z" />
          </svg>
          CRITICAL NOTICE: PLEASE READ CAREFULLY
        </h2>
        <p class="text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300 mb-0">
          Pasabaya.app is a <strong>free, volunteer-run, open-source community carpool matching project</strong> for private individuals already traveling along similar routes. We do not provide transportation, dispatch vehicles, employ drivers, inspect vehicles, or verify user identities. You choose your travel companions and are responsible for checking the arrangements and taking reasonable precautions before traveling. A profile, accepted seat request, community badge, or trip review is not a guarantee of safety.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          Pasabaya is operated by <strong>Artem Blazhievskii</strong> (<a id="terms_operator_github" href="https://github.com/ablzh" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">ablzh on GitHub</a>). Pasabaya is a volunteer project, not a company. In these Terms, "Pasabaya" or "the Service" means the platform, and "we", "us", or "our" refers to Artem Blazhievskii as its operator.
        </p>
        <p>
          By creating an account, browsing ride listings, publishing a ride post, requesting a seat, or otherwise accessing Pasabaya.app ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to all of these Terms, you must not access or use the Service.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, id: "terms_privacy_policy" %> explains how personal data is collected, used, shared, and retained. Accepting these Terms does not waive your data privacy rights or replace any separate consent required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">2. Eligibility &amp; User Representations</h2>
        <p>You must be at least <strong>18 years of age</strong> to register or use Pasabaya.app. By using the platform, you represent and warrant that:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>You have the legal capacity to enter into a binding agreement under Philippine law.</li>
          <li>You have never been convicted of a crime involving physical violence, harassment, sexual misconduct, extortion, theft, or any felony offense.</li>
          <li>If you offer a ride as a driver:
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li>You hold a valid, unexpired Philippine Driver's License appropriate for your vehicle classification.</li>
              <li>The vehicle you operate possesses current, valid Land Transportation Office (LTO) registration (Official Receipt and Certificate of Registration - OR/CR).</li>
              <li>The vehicle is covered by at least valid Compulsory Third Party Liability (CTPL) insurance as required by Philippine law.</li>
              <li>The vehicle is maintained in a safe, roadworthy mechanical condition.</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>These are your declarations. Pasabaya does not independently verify your age, identity, criminal history, license, vehicle registration, or insurance. Keep your account details accurate and your login credentials private.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">3. Nature of the Platform</h2>
        <p>
          Pasabaya provides tools for publishing one-time or recurring driver offers, requesting and accepting passenger seats, receiving route alerts, and coordinating trips. Drivers choose their routes, travel days, departure times, and available seats. Pasabaya does not operate vehicles or direct drivers' journeys.
        </p>
        <p>
          Drivers and passengers connect as independent private individuals. Any travel arrangement, route selection, meeting point, or schedule agreement is formed solely between the respective users. Pasabaya is not a party to any contract, arrangement, or understanding formed between users.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">4. Non-Commercial Expense Sharing &amp; Prohibition of Commercial Transport</h2>
        <p>
          Pasabaya is strictly dedicated to non-commercial carpooling between private individuals traveling toward a shared destination:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Voluntary Expense Sharing:</strong> Where permitted by applicable law, travelers may voluntarily agree to share actual, out-of-pocket travel expenses such as fuel and tolls. Contributions must relate to the shared journey and must not generate profit or remuneration for the driver. Agree any contribution before traveling.</li>
          <li><strong>Prohibition of Commercial Exploitation:</strong> Users are strictly prohibited from using Pasabaya to operate unauthorized public passenger transport ("colorum"), run taxi or shuttle services, offer commercial courier or cargo dispatch, or solicit fares for hire or reward.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct Peer Settlement:</strong> Any permitted contribution is agreed and settled directly between users outside Pasabaya. Pasabaya does not set contribution amounts, collect or enforce payment, or adjudicate payment disputes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Use of a free platform or sharing expenses does not establish an exemption from transport laws. Drivers must comply with applicable permit, franchise, licensing, registration, and insurance requirements. Pasabaya does not grant transport authority or insurance coverage.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">5. Platform Fees &amp; Payments</h2>
        <p>
          Pasabaya charges <strong>zero commission, zero booking fees, and zero service charges</strong> to drivers or passengers. The platform contains no in-app wallet, payment processing gateway, escrow mechanism, fare calculator, or dynamic rate engine. Pasabaya never receives, processes, collects, or disburses money on behalf of any user.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">6. Seat Requests, Recurring Rides &amp; Cancellations</h2>
        <p>
          All seat reservations on ride offers require explicit driver review and approval:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Requests &amp; Confirmation:</strong> Sending a seat request does not reserve a seat. A seat is confirmed only when the driver accepts the request while seats remain available and the trip and participants remain eligible. Drivers may accept or decline requests for lawful reasons, subject to the platform's availability and audience rules.</li>
          <li><strong>Recurring Offers:</strong> Drivers choose the weekdays and departure time in Philippine time. A regular ride makes individual departures available up to 14 days ahead. Without an end date, it repeats until paused or ended. Passengers must request a seat for each departure; acceptance does not reserve seats on other dates.</li>
          <li><strong>Schedule Changes:</strong> Editing a series does not automatically change departures that already have pending or accepted requests. Review those departures separately. Pausing a series stops new requests and expires pending requests while preserving accepted bookings. Resuming does not revive expired requests or canceled departures. Ending the series cancels its future departures, including accepted bookings.</li>
          <li><strong>Closing Requests &amp; Canceling:</strong> Closing a trip to new requests does not cancel accepted bookings. Drivers and passengers should use the cancellation controls promptly when they cannot travel and notify their companions. A confirmed booking can still be canceled; Pasabaya does not guarantee that a journey will take place.</li>
          <li><strong>Ladies Only Rides:</strong> These offers require a driver and passengers whose profiles are set to female. Gender is self-declared. This preference does <strong>not</strong> verify identity or guarantee personal safety.</li>
          <li><strong>Community Hub Rides:</strong> Rides posted within closed institutional hubs require email domain verification. Hub verification indicates that an institutional email address was verified; it does not constitute an endorsement, background investigation, or safety warranty by the institution or by Pasabaya.</li>
          <li><strong>Route Alerts:</strong> An optional route alert requests a one-time notification about a matching, available offer. It does not book a seat or guarantee that the offer will remain available when you open it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">7. In-App Coordination Chat &amp; Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>
          The driver and accepted passengers receive access to their trip's coordination chat. Pending and declined requesters cannot access it. Eligible previously confirmed participants may retain access for cancellation coordination. Bans, account deletion, and loss of required hub access revoke chat access.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Permitted Use:</strong> In-app chat must be used exclusively to coordinate trip logistics (such as pickup locations, delays, luggage capacity, and arrival estimates).</li>
          <li><strong>Prohibited Conduct:</strong> You must not send harassment, hate speech, threats, sexually explicit material, stalking messages, fraudulent requests, unauthorized advertising, or off-platform commercial solicitations.</li>
          <li><strong>Protect Your Information:</strong> Do not disclose bank account credentials, credit card details, e-wallet PINs, one-time passwords (OTPs), or government identity documents in chat. Share only what your companions need to coordinate the trip.</li>
          <li><strong>Messaging &amp; History Deadlines:</strong> Messaging closes 24 hours after the booking cutoff. If a trip is canceled while messaging is open, messaging closes 24 hours after cancellation. Cancellation does not reopen closed messaging or unavailable history. Authorized participants may read the conversation for another 30 days after messaging closes. At the history deadline, chat becomes inaccessible and deletion from the live database is scheduled. Background job delays can postpone physical deletion; backup copies follow the separate retention schedule in the Privacy Policy.</li>
          <li><strong>Privacy &amp; Moderation:</strong> Messages are protected in transit but are not end-to-end encrypted. Staff do not routinely monitor trip chat. Access may be necessary to investigate reported abuse, protect lawful rights, or comply with valid legal requirements, subject to applicable law and the retention deadlines. See the <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, id: "terms_chat_privacy" %> for details.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">8. Reliability, No-Show Incidents &amp; Account Freezes</h2>
        <p>
          Community punctuality and accountability are essential for peer-to-peer carpooling:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Mutual Reliability:</strong> Both drivers and passengers must arrive punctually at agreed meeting spots or notify companions in advance if unexpected delays arise.</li>
          <li><strong>Reporting &amp; Review:</strong> After a trip's departure, eligible participants may record trip outcomes and report a no-show. A report is an allegation, not a confirmed strike. An eligible administrator reviews the incident, records a reason for confirming or dismissing it, and notifies the reported account. Decisions can be corrected, with earlier decisions retained in the history. Submit reports honestly and avoid unnecessary personal information.</li>
          <li><strong>60-Day Rolling Window &amp; Temporary Freezes:</strong> We count upheld no-show incidents in a <strong>rolling 60-day window</strong>. A decision that brings an account to three (3) or more upheld incidents triggers a <strong>7-day freeze</strong> if it is not already frozen. During the freeze, the user cannot publish new offers, request seats, or accept new bookings. Active recurring schedules are paused. Existing accepted bookings are preserved, and a freeze alone does not remove otherwise authorized chat access. A paused schedule requires the driver's explicit action to resume after restrictions end.</li>
          <li><strong>Questions About a Decision:</strong> Contact <a id="terms_decision_contact" href="mailto:legal@pasabaya.app" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">legal@pasabaya.app</a> with the relevant trip and decision details if you believe a decision is incorrect. Repeated or serious misconduct may lead to further restrictions or account termination.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">9. Assumption of Risk &amp; Safety Due Diligence</h2>
        <p class="font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
          Traveling with other users involves risks. Consider the arrangements and your own circumstances before accepting or joining a ride.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pasabaya does not conduct criminal background checks, license verification, or vehicle safety inspections. Take reasonable precautions before traveling:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>Meet in well-lit, public areas with visible foot traffic.</li>
          <li>Inspect the driver's license, vehicle plates, and registration documents before boarding.</li>
          <li>Share your ride details, route, and companion information with family members or trusted emergency contacts.</li>
          <li>Decline to board or leave immediately if you feel unsafe or observe signs of intoxication or reckless behavior.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

